Some people would put a space between "le" and "nu", while others would
write it as "lenu".
The cmavo list seems to be saying that "ledo ..." or "lemi ..." etc. is
respectively a distinctive vocabulary differing from "le do ..." or "le mi
...".
The same question goes for the comparison between ".i se ri'a bo ..." and
".iseri'abo ...", for example.
Is it just a matter of personal preference or is there some particular
signification in it?

